WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.900
Good morning, Hank, as you can tell by the grey speckled walls behind me, I'm in an airport.

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.140
It's Question Tuesday, the day that I answer real questions

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:09.200
from real Nerdfighters. Today I'm going to answer questions about

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.060
love, and sex.

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:12.880
When do you think it's okay to lose your virginity?

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:16.380
You know, call me old fashioned, but I don't think 34 year old men vlogging in airports should

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:18.100
decide when other people have sex.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.500
I like this guy and I think he likes me back, but I'm not sure. How do I find out for sure?

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.000
I'm gonna tell you what I tell Henry several times a day:

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.720
"Use your words!"

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.900
Just talk to him - if you start going out you're going to have to talk to him anyways.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.480
There's a girl in my school who I like but I don't exactly know-

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.440
JUST ASK HER using your words! You're not an Avox!

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.880
Wait - or are you? If you're an Avox, write it down.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:38.020
What is your stand on birth control pills?

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:41.600
I try not to stand on birth control pills at all; I think it might decrease their effectiveness.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:44.060
How do you say no to sex without offending your partner?

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:45.860
To answer your question, lets make a Venn Diagram.

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:47.480
Let this circle be asshats

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.280
and here are the people who get offended when you say no to sex.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:52.280
Do you think it matters how many people someone has slept with?

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:55.800
No, and it particularly bothers me that women are held to a different standard on this front than men.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.380
Also, it's such a weird thing to care about. Like, imagine if I started eating cheerios for breakfast

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:04.460
would cheerios be like "I'm the 48th cereal you've tried eating, I don't feel special!"

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:08.900
Well, then screw you cheerios I can't go into the past and un-eat all those cereals but that doesn't mean

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:11.200
I don't genuinely enjoy your whole grain crunch.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:12.760
How do I know he's the "one"?

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:15.760
I don't think there is one "one". Have you ever had a crush on a band member?

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:18.620
Let me ask your question with a question: is Toby Turner in a band?

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:19.540
John, do you ship wholock?

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:21.980
Sometimes I feel like you guys just make up words to confuse me.

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:23.980
When is it too soon to say "I love you?"

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:25.980
Just remember you can't un-ring that bell.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:27.980
Have you ever wanted to experience giving birth?

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:30.680
No, I've seen birth.

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:34.480
No. Yeah, no. No, no, no...no.

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:36.480
Is there a way to tell if he actually cares or if he just

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:37.640
wants a hookup?

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:38.700
Yeah is he a douchebag?

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.780
The first time you saw the Yeti, did you think she was the one?

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:42.780
No, the first time I saw the Yeti she was in 8th grade

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:45.520
and I did not think, 'Oh I'm gonna marry that 8th grader!'

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:47.520
What do you think of an "Othello" kind of love?

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.820
You mean the kind where you beat up the love of your life and then kill her?

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:51.820
I'm opposed to it.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:53.820
In your opinion, is pre-marital sex wrong?

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:56.740
I certainly don't think there's anything inherently wrong with pre-marital sex.

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:59.000
Like for example, it's legal for gay people to be married in some states

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.480
but not in others and it's a little bit ridiculous to say that it's possible

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:05.180
for gay people to have morally justifiable sex in Vermont

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:07.180
but not in Mississippi.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:08.940
Frankly, I don't really see it as my job to tell people

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:11.180
who they should have sex with or under what circumstances.

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:14.080
Also this is an awkward thing to talk about in an airport.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:16.120
*sings* The people in the airport think that I'm crazy.

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:19.420
The people in the airport think that I'm crazy.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:22.300
And maybe I am to be fair.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.140
What is the secret to a successful marriage?

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:26.960
Mutual generosity, also it's nice that you can like the same television programs.

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:29.240
Is it wrong to do gay stuff, like just kissing?

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:31.020
Aw man, your question makes me so sad.

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:33.240
No, of course it's not wrong. If you wanna kiss someone

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:36.400
and that person wants to kiss you back that is awesome.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.400
And don't let anyone tell you you should be ashamed about that.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:42.080
People are so ashamed about their sexuality but you shouldn't be.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:42.820
It's great!

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:46.060
I'm talking about it in Terminal A of the  Indianapolis airport.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:48.360
On average, what animal takes the longest to copulate?

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:51.540
I don't know, but I do know that llama sex lasts like two hours

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:54.180
because male llamas experience something called "dribble ejaculation".

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:55.320
How do I know these things?

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:57.320
He loves me and I don't love him and he won't take

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:58.460
no for an answer?

00:02:58.460 --> 00:02:59.520
Yeah, then he doesn't love you.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:02.460
He doesn't even respect your right to choose your own romantic partners.

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:04.780
Is it weird that I'm in college and I've never kissed anyone?

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:06.780
Not at all, as evidenced by the fact that your question was the most

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:09.940
